===Head to the Divination Commission and ask for help from Fu Xuan{{subst:void|<!--202050112-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Divination Commission|update|After witnessing the wonders of the Matrix of Prescience Ultima, March 7th couldn't get the idea of using it to re-discover her past out of her head. She decides to ask for the master diviner's help with fulfilling this wish of hers.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
;(По прибытии на место)

;(По прибытии на место)
:'''March 7th:''' Good morning! Is work going well today, master diviner?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I am extremely busy of late. If you have something to ask of me, do not delay.
:'''March 7th:''' ...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' You were about to say something along the lines of: "How did you know I wanted to ask something?" &mdash; but then you remembered who you were talking to and decided not to bother, correct?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You really do live up to your title.
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Of course &mdash; I run a dozen hexagrams before I even get around to breakfast. The results are never far wrong.
::Well, the look on her face says it all, doesn't it?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Well, the look on her face says it all, doesn't it?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' A face is not a reliable instrument of divination. On the contrary, I run a dozen hexagrams before I even get around to breakfast. The results are never far wrong.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Today's divinations threw up some unexpected complications &mdash; the hexagrammatic position was vacillating between the water and heaven trigrams. The Matrix of Prescience gave the following interpretation: "You will have three uninvited guests. This is ultimately auspicious."
:{{tx}}
----
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Mm, I see. You wish to use the Matrix to relive the past and awaken parts of your memory? Viable in principle, but whether the Matrix is truly capable of achieving this result remains to be seen.
:'''March 7th:''' *sigh* I knew it. Things are never simple are they...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But with Kafka...
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Kafka's situation was different.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Not even the omniscient master diviner can make it happen?
::'''Fu Xuan:''' Wh&mdash;Who said that? I didn't say it was impossible, I said it was "viable in principle." There is a gap of a million light-years between impossibility and viability.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I feel like I must explain in detail the principles behind the Divination Commission's ultimate weapon to avoid any misunderstandings...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' The Matrix of Prescience does not allow one to remember anything. It merely collects data in order to infer "past events" &mdash; in the same way that "future events" are inferred.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Just as Realm-Keeping Commission officers collect forensic evidence to recreate the scene of a crime, there are materials from which we can infer the past. These may be items related to the experience, or memories of the people involved.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Miss March's predicament is very different from Kafka's situation, because she doesn't remember what happened in her past.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I am no medical professional... but fortunately I'm very fond of reading! We understand that there are two types of memory loss: One where the memories remain dormant, floating around in the unconsciousness unable to be awakened, and another that involves direct erasure of memories from the brain...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Unable to be awakened...
::'''March 7th:''' Something must have happened when I was frozen in the ice. I bet the memories were freezing and decided to hibernate.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Someone erased March's memory...
::'''March 7th:''' Ah!? Who would do such a horrible mean thing!?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Why don't we try using the Matrix of Prescience to determine which situation pertains to Miss March?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Let's begin then by preparing the requisite inference materials. Miss March, your memory is unreliable. To guarantee the Matrix's accuracy, you'll have to provide something related to your past experience... anything will do.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' When you're ready, come and find me in the Matrix core.
----
:'''March 7th:''' The diviner said I need to provide something from my past experiences...
:'''March 7th:''' Hmm, what should it be? How about a Xianzhou souvenir?
{{Dialogue End}}

===Chat with Fu Xuan about how to search for lost memories{{subst:void|<!--202050104-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Divination Commission|update|Fu Xuan is not opposed to the request to use the Matrix of Prescience Ultima to deduce the past. Seems like this isn't her first time helping someone with something like this.<br />As long as enough data is provided to support its calculations, deducing the past is the same as predicting the future for the Matrix of Prescience.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

;(Talk to Fu Xuan)
----
:'''Fu Xuan:''' So, have you acquired something from your past? As a Nameless, surely you must have souvenirs from your journeys that could evoke memories?
:'''March 7th:''' I've got lots! It's just, I don't know what to choose.
